                "fallback": "A presidential executive order on homelessness released this summer promotes punitive policies toward people who are unsheltered across the country — loosening involuntary institutionalization laws… | Steinberg Institute",
                "text": "A presidential executive order on homelessness released this summer promotes punitive policies toward people who are unsheltered across the country — loosening involuntary institutionalization laws and prioritizing funding for cities that impose stricter measures on encampments and involuntary holds.\n\nIn a recent San Francisco Public Press article, our Director of Government Affairs, Tara Gamboa-Eastman, MPP, discusses how this order could reshape California’s behavioral health system. She highlights its emphasis on institutionalization and criminalization, and worries that evidence-based community programs could lose funding as a result.\n\nStill, California remains steadfast in its commitment to building a more compassionate, accessible behavioral health system. As Tara says, “We are really trying to come from a place of not giving in to anticipatory compliance and preserving that vision until we’re told otherwise.”\n\nRead the full article: <https:\/\/lnkd.in\/eWaPvc47>",
